Lab 18: Setting Up Network Policies for Virtual Machines
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Configure network policies to control traffic flow between virtual machines
Implement network isolation between different VM networks using iptables and network namespaces
Test and validate network policy functionality through practical communication tests
Understand the security implications of VM network segmentation
Troubleshoot common network policy configuration issues
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command line operations
Familiarity with virtual machine concepts
Knowledge of basic networking principles (IP addresses, subnets, routing)
Understanding of iptables firewall rules (basic level)
Experience with SSH and remote system administration
Required Knowledge Areas:
Linux system administration fundamentals
Basic virtualization concepts
Network security principles
Command-line text editors (nano, vim, or similar)
