Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: VMs Not Getting IP Addresses
Symptoms: VMs start but don't receive IP addresses from DHCP

Solution:

# Restart libvirt networks
sudo virsh net-destroy production-net
sudo virsh net-start production-net
sudo virsh net-destroy development-net  
sudo virsh net-start development-net

# Restart VMs
sudo virsh reboot production-vm
sudo virsh reboot development-vm
Issue 2: iptables Rules Not Working
Symptoms: Network policies not blocking traffic as expected

Solution:

# Check if rules are in correct order
sudo iptables -L FORWARD -n --line-numbers

# Ensure custom chain is being called
sudo iptables -L -n | grep VM_NETWORK_POLICY

# Reload rules if needed
sudo iptables-restore < /etc/iptables/rules.v4
Issue 3: SSH Connection Issues
Symptoms: Cannot SSH to VMs for testing

Solution:

# Check VM console access
sudo virsh console production-vm
# (Press Ctrl+] to exit console)

# Verify SSH service is running in VM
ssh -i ~/.ssh/lab_key labuser@$PROD_VM_IP "sudo systemctl status ssh"

# Check firewall on VMs
ssh -i ~/.ssh/lab_key labuser@$PROD_VM_IP "sudo ufw status"
Issue 4: Network Bridges Not Working
Symptoms: VMs cannot communicate with host or external networks

Solution:

# Check bridge status
ip addr show | grep virbr

# Restart networking
sudo systemctl restart libvirtd

# Verify bridge forwarding
cat /proc/sys/net/ipv4/ip_forward
# Should return 1, if not:
echo 1 | sudo tee /proc/sys/net/ipv4/ip_forward
